diff --git a/tpp06/README.md b/tpp06/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c4553b6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tpp06/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# TPP06 Linux port
+
+This directory contains the non-destructive bring-up work for running the
+Linux/fbdev build of openHASP on the Tuya/MOES TPP06 (Anyka AK3761).
+
+The first milestone only probes `/dev/fb0` and the Linux input devices. It does
+not stop Tuya, overwrite the framebuffer, change startup scripts, or write to
+the panel filesystem outside a temporary upload.
+
+Known hardware on the tested panel:
+
+- ARM926EJ-S (`armv5tejl`), Linux 4.4;
+- 320 x 480, BGR565 framebuffer at `/dev/fb0`;
+- Goodix touchscreen at `/dev/input/event1`;
+- GPIO keys at `/dev/input/event0`.
+
+Build the static probe:
+
+```sh
+./tpp06/build-probe.sh
+```
+
+The output is `build-tpp06/tpp06-probe`.
+
+Set `TPP06_TOOLCHAIN_DIR` to the Bootlin ARMv5 uClibc toolchain directory when
+it is not installed at the development-machine default. `PIO` can similarly
+point to the PlatformIO executable.
+
+Build the static openHASP port (including the Goodix multitouch and BGR565
+fixes):
+
+```sh
+./tpp06/build-openhasp.sh
+```
+
+The output is `build-tpp06/openhasp-tpp06`. It is an ARM EABI5,
+soft-float, statically linked binary. The current bring-up runs it manually
+from `/tmp`; it must not be installed as a boot service until display, touch,
+MQTT, and rollback tests are complete.
+
+`runtime/` contains a safe MQTT configuration template, a 320 x 480 test page,
+and a separate RGB/orientation calibration page. Never commit a real MQTT
+password.
+
+`tools/fb565_to_png.py` converts a raw 307200-byte framebuffer capture to PNG.
+`tools/tcp_receive.py` is a one-shot receiver for copying captures from the
+panel's BusyBox `nc` over a trusted LAN.
+
+See [STATUS.md](STATUS.md) for the validated hardware and remaining work.
